{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.collatz_vtwo_domain_rescope","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.collatz_vtwo_domain_rescope","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.QCollatz"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_vTwo_witness_escapes_domain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_vTwo_witness_escapes_domain","kind":"theorem","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_vtwo_domain_rescope.lean#L35-L54","doc":"**The `v_[2]` witness `-X-2` escapes the domain at step 4.**  The four\nbranch-defining relations chain `-X-2 → -(X+1)² → -(X+1) → -1 → -X` (odd,\neven, even, odd), and `-X` satisfies neither the `q`-even (`[2]_q ∣ -X`) nor\nthe `q`-odd (`[2]_q ∣ -X+1`) condition — so it is outside the domain of the\npartial Skein-Collatz map. Therefore the witness is **not** domain-stable,\nand the `v_[2]`-increase it exhibits lies outside the cone `D∞` where the\nconjecture is posed. ","signatureChunk":0}]}